    "who": "MANAN",
    "text": "So the limit isn't my body. It's your judgement. They call it the Central Governor Theory.",
    "fr": 178,
    "in": 1424,
    "out": 1602,
    "trans": "ON SCREEN SUBTITLE, small, low in frame, held two seconds, nobody speaks it:\n\"Central Governor Theory, proposed by Prof. Tim Noakes, 1997. An influential model. Scientists are still investigating how the brain and muscles produce fatigue.\"\nIt costs no running time because it is not spoken, and it is what protects the film on scientific accuracy.",
